<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caledon River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mohokare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Caledon River, Mohokare in Sesotho, rises in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a> and flows south-west for about 480 km to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a>. For much of its course it forms the border between Lesotho and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s Free State. Its fertile valley was fought over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a>, the Batlokwa and the Orange Free State in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caledon-river.jpg" alt="Caledon River" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graham Maclachlan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_Old_railway_bridge....._-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
